# LF in the repository and LF in every working tree, Windows included.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true and the CI runner keeps that default, so
# without this line the Windows job checks out sources whose lines end in CRLF. The tests that
# read the repository's own text then look for a blank line ("\n\n") that no longer exists —
# the ProblemKind table is parsed out of src/types.ts that way — and the bundle built there
# would ship CRLF to every user. `text=auto` still leaves the pictures alone: Git detects a
# binary file by its content, not by this rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
